Why: cscc/ilrun shortcut.  Mono's build passes csc's /codepage:65001 (the 
Windows code page number of UTF-8).  cscc's csc-compatibility mode defaults 
to the Latin-1 charset and only recognised '/codepage:utf8' as UTF-8, so 
with /codepage:65001 the UTF-8 BOM handling in the C# pre-processor is off 
and every mcs source file that starts with a BOM fails ('parse error at or 
near' the BOM byte; argument.cs, context.cs, dynamic.cs of mono-2.6.4).  
Treat 65001 like utf8.  New patch (not in Guix).

diff --git a/cscc/common/cc_compat.c b/cscc/common/cc_compat.c
index b05421f..3141bb0 100644
--- a/cscc/common/cc_compat.c
+++ b/cscc/common/cc_compat.c
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@ static void codepageOption(char *arg)
 	{
 		latin1_charset = 1;
 	}
-	else if(!ILStrICmp(arg, "utf8"))
+	else if(!ILStrICmp(arg, "utf8") || !ILStrICmp(arg, "65001"))
 	{
 		latin1_charset = 0;
 	}
